# Zoom speaking notes

When the user asks for a **script**, talking points, what to say, or notes for a
hearing / CMC / Zoom appearance:

- Follow `.claude/skills/hearing-script/SKILL.md`.
- The chat is a **glanceable Zoom card**, not a teleprompter.
- Never use "If they say…", "Q. / A.", "Point A", "Read this", or complete
  "Your Honor, …" paragraphs in anything he might have open on camera.
- Opening he can say without looking down. Then 3–6 word cues. One-line ask.
- One screen. No scrolling. No PDF unless he asks.
- Full argument and traps only if he asks for homework, in a separate artifact
  labeled `DO NOT OPEN ON CAMERA`.

Locked after the August 28, 2026 CHP demurrer (Matter 20). The Court could tell.
